From 1cebba33c06ab9c75bda95954c2a2aab44901688 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shaurizard <contact@nyoom.engineering>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 12:21:12 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 45/48] feat(audio): let audio drivers play host-format streams

Xenia Canary's title-playlist player (AudioMediaPlayer) decodes WMA and
MP3 files on the host and feeds the PCM to an audio driver that the
audio system creates outside the guest client table. The ReXGlue driver
interface could not take that: AudioDriver::SubmitFrame took a guest
address, SDLAudioDriver was fixed at 6 channels of 48 kHz big-endian
guest render frames, and nothing could pause or attenuate one driver.

This brings the interface to Canary's shape (Canary 451f915,
src/xenia/apu/audio_driver.h, sdl/sdl_audio_driver.cc,
audio_system.h, nop/nop_audio_system.cc):

- AudioDriver gets the kFrame* constants, virtual Initialize/Shutdown,
  SubmitFrame(float*) on a host pointer, Pause, Resume and SetVolume.
  AudioSystem::SubmitFrame translates the guest address itself, so the
  driver no longer needs the Memory pointer.
- AudioSystem::CreateDriver(semaphore, frequency, channels,
  need_format_conversion) creates an unregistered driver. SDL returns an
  SDLAudioDriver; Nop returns Canary's PacingAudioDriver, which discards
  frames and releases their semaphore slots at the playback rate so a
  player keeps real time with no output device. PacingAudioDriver is
  ported unchanged apart from the threading namespace.
- SDLAudioDriver keeps the guest-format path as it was. With
  need_format_conversion false it opens the device stream at the
  source rate and channel count in native float and lets SDL resample
  and remap on its device thread. Each frame holds kFrameSamplesMax
  floats, as in Canary (768 samples of stereo).

Differences from Canary, which uses SDL2:

- Volume and the audio_mute cvar go through SDL_SetAudioStreamGain,
  multiplied by the existing output gain, instead of SDL_MixAudioFormat
  into a cleared buffer. The frames are put on the stream without a
  copy, and a volume change also reaches audio SDL has already queued.
- An empty queue is left short instead of padded with silence; the SDL3
  device thread pads short reads itself, and queued silence would only
  delay the next frame.
- A frame SDL refuses still releases its semaphore slot, so the
  producer cannot block on it forever.

Pause and Resume use SDL_PauseAudioStreamDevice and
SDL_ResumeAudioStreamDevice. The frame pool still grows on demand, but
the semaphore bounds the number of frames in flight, so it stops
allocating once it covers that budget.

Co-authored-by: factory-droid[bot] <138933559+factory-droid[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>
